From ad4b86f2dd94593dc25796aa788fdc3d1b6eb3c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Stewart <peter@stewartmail.xyz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:10:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] vcomp: Implement _vcomp_for_dynamic_init_i8 and
 _vcomp_for_dynamic_next_i8.

The 64-bit loop index variants of the dynamic schedule functions were stubs, so
64-bit code using schedule(dynamic) or schedule(runtime) with a 64-bit index
aborted. JM Studio's TextureMapping_release.dll calls them.

The dynamic state is widened to 64 bits and shared with the 32-bit functions;
those still compute their iteration count in 32 bits and truncate the bounds
they return, so their wraparound behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
